<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Installation Guide · Let's DANE</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <div class="logo">
      <span class="icon">🔒</span>
      <div>
        <h1>Installation Guide</h1>
        <p>Firefox-first · Local CA only</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a href="/" class="status-badge">← Dashboard</a>
  </header>
  <main>
    <section class="section">
      <h2>1. Download the Root CA</h2>
      <p>From the main dashboard, download the PEM certificate.</p>
      <a href="/api/ca/cert.pem" class="download-btn" download>Download letsdane-ca.crt (PEM)</a>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>2. Import into Firefox (recommended primary target)</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open Firefox → Settings</li>
        <li>Privacy & Security → Certificates → View Certificates</li>
        <li>Authorities tab → Import</li>
        <li>Select the downloaded <code>letsdane-ca.crt</code></li>
        <li>Check <strong>“Trust this CA to identify websites”</strong></li>
        <li>OK</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>3. Configure the proxy</h2>
      <p>Point Firefox (or system) to the local proxy:</p>
      <p class="mono">HTTP/HTTPS Proxy: 127.0.0.1 port 8080</p>
      <p>In Firefox: Settings → Network Settings → Manual proxy configuration.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Other browsers / OS (later)</h2>
      <p>Chrome/Brave: use the same CA but install via OS trust store or chrome://settings/certificates.</p>
      <p>Windows/macOS/Linux system stores: more invasive; Firefox-first is preferred for testing.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Security reminders</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The private key never leaves this machine.</li>
        <li>Only the public certificate is downloadable.</li>
        <li>Dashboard and proxy bind only to 127.0.0.1.</li>
        <li>DNSSEC/TLSA failure is fail-closed (no silent fallback).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
